      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay so start() being called here means that when this handler thread starts, the IkeV2VpnRunner instance is not actually finished building, so unless you have an edge somewhere it is not obliged to observe this object as being constructed. While start() is such an edge with respect to mProfile, mIpSecManager and mNetworkCallback, you don\u0027t have such an edge for \u0027this\u0027, making the whole enterprise a bit adventurous.",
      "range": {
