        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-30T09:55:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ouch, what happened to final ? Can\u0027t you create the thread in the constructor for LegacyVpnRunner instead of taking this kind of audacious (to say the least) risk ? Don\u0027t call start() in the constructor though – you wouldn\u0027t have a happens-before relationship between the freeze and code running in the thread – but have expose start() method in LegacyVpnRunner that you\u0027ll call from l.2080.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2589,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2589,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "d70860d546cf388eb1d185f80692f1cbee971ce9",
